diffs.patch:
Index: openwiki/.claims/security.json
===================================================================
--- openwiki/.claims/security.json	
+++ openwiki/.claims/security.json	
@@ -0,0 +1,128 @@
+{
+  "schemaVersion": 1,
+  "pageVersion": "sha256:a4253b260ed6a5a532a5df838c6713bac7db7fdeeb1919b2bf0c8640b7c929b3",
+  "claims": [
+    {
+      "id": "claim_d52ac93ec1064385906001f3e7dbf061",
+      "statement": "celld trusts the application code, the fleet nodes, and the operators; it is not safe for hostile multi-tenant use, and security fixes apply to the latest release only.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/security.md#L3-L12",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:527aadab3085ed77e0ba1e9e86f6050df8460764231978cba9e21b0105358ef9:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_8c9630e1a5b6401f8a18041955fa5311",
+      "statement": "celld depends on a trusted private network and object storage credentials as its external security boundaries, and does not terminate TLS on either listener.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/security.md#L13-L18",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7db00d70deef36aa090e544202181f33fab53b28170a5b3883b0cdf86cfd6d69:"
+        },
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/security.md#L82-L85",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c15410dececc616e9bf0b2f72b2285c515b7ab528fc4df98dc92a1ec00ada9ac:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_39952269cb174b53b72d48785aeaf6e0",
+      "statement": "celld opens two HTTP listeners: the public Worker listener (--listen) and the internal peer/operator listener (--internal-listen) that defaults to 127.0.0.1:0; the public listener reserves only /.well-known/celld/health and the internal listener returns 404 for unknown paths rather than passing them to the Worker.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/security.md#L21-L45",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:64a705b6105962b15f3a010ead1d1f4fc1b6d931a0b466f0286bc632920209ac:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_bd5b382b4a264eec96022b7f56448ece",
+      "statement": "The fleet HMAC authenticates peer-control and reserved-cell operator requests with a clock limit and replay protection, and the peer tunnel establishment request carries it so only a holder of the fleet secret can open a tunnel.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/security.md#L59-L77",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c44e39377c8734a1e520e2ecdff61100645113b920ade049ab1217245a466689:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_b7f0a181ced0498d917db7184c2eb32e",
+      "statement": "The clock window is two-sided (30 seconds) and replay retention must be at least the clock window, enforced as pure predicates in crates/logic/peer.rs so the replay hole cannot reopen.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/peer_auth.rs#L25-L30",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:58abd41c53310c42ff3eec8caed852ca8a42ec7b5bb9d58e8bd66693905c5ad0:"
+        },
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/peer.rs#L23-L37",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:222fbbe1b56b3e2da2cf0dc17f1e19768b629f3ebc6cc61d9e82121643ee8ba7:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_12a4cfad0316470191d70728f85642d5",
+      "statement": "The peer-authentication identity charset restricts source and target to non-empty ASCII alphanumerics plus _ - . at most 128 bytes, so a target cannot smuggle a path segment past the WrongTarget check.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/peer.rs#L17-L22",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:049d3cf81f89e85ba83d5b475dcdcd7de6c45a22fb9bf4a19a61a038a7b5f254:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_951779c891004347a0d7b46ae3aa2e5d",
+      "statement": "The unauthenticated internal operator routes are /state, /cell/<SCOPE>, /evict/<SCOPE>, /do/<ID>, and POST /shutdown; the /do/ route refuses every reserved runtime class, which instead route through the HMAC-authenticated /runtime/<SCOPE>.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/security.md#L87-L99",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d48f3f630de3083d1f3b811813ee01751ba1cb7114cec00286e59f37d1b71530:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_9880c2d4ce5f4dda8656ecc9d094120b",
+      "statement": "Without a trusted proxy the Host header controls the hostname in request.url; celld accepts a hostname, IPv4, or bracketed IPv6 with optional port, rejects malformed values, and uses celld.local when no source gives a valid host.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/security.md#L116-L124",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:857adde0799dc9043c86826e8d06f595aff14745f177f7f74cf20bdb236eecfe:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_f028007989694db3bfb70165f84962df",
+      "statement": "The public Worker listener and /do/<ID> have a 1 GiB default body limit (changed by CELLD_MAX_REQUEST_BODY_BYTES), and celld returns 413 for a declared oversized body and when a Worker reads past the limit.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/security.md#L126-L135",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ecb070d98423e69f8f9154c4b712e70c4ade512c2daea20b52e509050cadb05d:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_8402260fed5247acae484b240149e25b",
+      "statement": "The fleet bucket is the root of authority for the fleet, storing the deployments, cell state, ownership leases, node leases, and the peer-authentication secret; a holder of the bucket credentials controls the fleet.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/security.md#L139-L145",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b14fd7a6d72fae36830fc94437be7b2af24def7d96fbc379c3e4ba806f0631ee:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_837b4ecbde69449180cbb907abab1206",
+      "statement": "A cell scope is a security fence: valid_cell_scope restricts it to ASCII alphanumerics plus _ - . : $ at most 255 bytes and rejects . and .., so a scope can never be more than one path component and cannot escape the data directory or the bucket prefix.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/cell.rs#L28-L45",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1f73910a09630b835559786177ffe25cbfa37327e86cbf826c7cb0b718b78745:"
+        }
+      ]
+    }
+  ],
+  "verification": {
+    "by": "openwiki/0.4.3",
+    "at": "2026-09-12T21:30:17.310Z"
+  }
+}

Index: openwiki/.claims/storage.json
===================================================================
--- openwiki/.claims/storage.json	
+++ openwiki/.claims/storage.json	
@@ -0,0 +1,110 @@
+{
+  "schemaVersion": 1,
+  "pageVersion": "sha256:3406a1aed81b281e07cf72b1a96d2475db37110d924aa9913a64274ff7d8a377",
+  "claims": [
+    {
+      "id": "claim_cc826ee72d784d02854e9200b60bbd4c",
+      "statement": "The bucket client is the engine's single object-store client bound to one bucket, speaking the object_store crate dialect with all bodies in-memory Bytes, and it treats the CAS token as an opaque String a conditional write consumes.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/bucket.rs#L3-L12",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fa78ce41373473691ce8be493059ab229d2c532e7513eb632535287b7ba4c668:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_d2a7276112b5457db768a05f9bc69303",
+      "statement": "There are two conditional-write dialects: s3:// and az:// speak the etag dialect (If-Match/If-None-Match), while gs:// speaks the Cloud Storage XML API dialect with x-goog-if-generation-match and OAuth; the distinction is the dialect, not the endpoint.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/bucket.rs#L5-L11",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2fb1cfd0a8349ff77d5f4f774b07855fa23cda1c1ac5f757e8e2e2cb9f76d651:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_4597da0850374ec4be4ec3e9d6417539",
+      "statement": "put_cas answers Ok(None) only for a clean 412/409 rejection and every other failure is ambiguous; a response carrying no CAS token is an error, so a stale owner's late write cannot be mistaken for a clean rejection.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/bucket.rs#L13-L17",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:64bb5fde8f277347824984d41a423caa949e7e449b3b6e861ad2f075f2c7bf9b:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_d1561afaa76d400bbd6826e2a9f1ce2e",
+      "statement": "S3-compatible storage uses the standard AWS credential chain (with EKS Pod Identity support), Google Cloud Storage uses Application Default Credentials, and Azure Blob Storage requires exactly one credential family: account key, managed identity, or workload identity.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/README.md#L128-L179",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e2fc2d1e841e288fd412636e0a6c89e8ffc7a81f858f8bab3b59eeb64ba79bb8:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_958d2aa3ac954eac8d3703db7605a9ff",
+      "statement": "celld reserves the probe/, cells/, nodes/, node-cells/, fleet/, deploy/, deploy-blobs/, wake/, drain/, log/, and telemetry/ prefixes and deletes objects under some of them, so an application must not write under these prefixes.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/guarantees.md#L78-L81",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:20f67018001ec0d74645b241a61691ebcf6b71f9236f3b1d3987094e055609e9:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_fe7de178340e486991cc6c66867d23b6",
+      "statement": "The storage test sends four conditional writes and requires two to fail; each node repeats it once at startup and stops on a broken store, and it can be disabled with CELLD_STORAGE_PROBE=0.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/guarantees.md#L60-L74",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:892e1eb818e0ce401e56b81b831115c33da069011ca4175a12b8240f6bc1831a:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_2f7004de14124b52bd50d962fb070876",
+      "statement": "A bucket value can carry a key prefix (s3://BUCKET/PREFIX) so two fleets can share one bucket; a bucket value without a prefix keeps objects at the root so an existing fleet does not move its data.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/README.md#L205-L207",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:81b028689e5df1c52bc8fe4f71fd99ab56a3a3b1ae5435bd44857f8a5aa9b0ac:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_833f62f6fa1c4959a6fd271b9e5b59c1",
+      "statement": "Each cell's durable data lives under cells/<cell>/ltx/e<epoch>/ in the bucket, mirroring the local watch/<cell>/ltx/e<epoch>/db.sqlite tree, and the in-process replica carries the fleet's key prefix itself so two fleets sharing one bucket do not replicate over each other.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/ltx_repl.rs#L9-L15",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e5fd77dfd54d80c86345889b819dd76655ac1c4ccc646c442c33fe38595381cc:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_352c1a8d5d6e44ed91804ef3242942f5",
+      "statement": "MinIO (community edition) passes the storage test but is not production-qualified, and one broken release (RELEASE.2025-09-06T17-38-46Z) rejects the conditional create of an absent object.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/guarantees.md#L36-L41",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c8fc9b60d6a21c2ee33ccf93a46fef573a34c0dddd7f4da8b2fc22c9493ea264:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_59d222684d5a441c89028bf0e96eb3ea",
+      "statement": "The ownership-store adapter contains only serialization, wall-clock sampling, SDK configuration, and error classification; ownership decisions remain in celld-logic.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/ownership_store.rs#L3-L8",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:692a8b13a42c6216a5dfdea1b9352eeec417cf39c1260245464eaf53b664dceb:"
+        }
+      ]
+    }
+  ],
+  "verification": {
+    "by": "openwiki/0.4.3",
+    "at": "2026-09-12T21:30:17.310Z"
+  }
+}

Index: openwiki/.claims/telemetry.json
===================================================================
--- openwiki/.claims/telemetry.json	
+++ openwiki/.claims/telemetry.json	
@@ -0,0 +1,124 @@
+{
+  "schemaVersion": 1,
+  "pageVersion": "sha256:e1da965c15583da011b605df9988f9f62b0539c26d631fbfd3a3e733ca978975",
+  "claims": [
+    {
+      "id": "claim_0fa461035d8b4957891b90196fdfeabc",
+      "statement": "Telemetry is off by default and the off state costs nothing: init never runs, start_trace answers None, and no event is ever built; CELLD_OTEL=1 enables it.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/telemetry.rs#L16-L23",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:dca11f279ad70ecf5dacd490d0e2b638a6d023202a2504fa1d2b659c7b7415c2:"
+        },
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/telemetry.md#L3-L5",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1bf4214fa526dada1cd5b5edb5f262968f1439a8460733fbe17c4f824aaa6e5d:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_7b4f19d7ab65414dbdbabbbbfec9361b",
+      "statement": "The default sink writes Parquet under the telemetry/ prefix of a bucket and requires a fleet bucket, while the otlp sink sends OTLP/HTTP protobuf to a collector and works without one.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/telemetry.md#L6-L57",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5d29ef46ababcc87024300fa22b14c11d443ed583ca0f0e6a3d7708ade29adc6:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_7dc19d7257c84ff1a529645b0faff508",
+      "statement": "The telemetry schema is v0-unstable and each file carries the schema version in its object metadata; column names can change before a stable release.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/telemetry.md#L12-L14",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:38c8ea3d475195d33f24bacf0b575d3ace2578b30bf0ff09fff3b1a778618c29:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_bd3119645cbd4186b7157fa410d6ee3e",
+      "statement": "celld records a span for each Worker fetch, each cell event (fetch, alarm, RPC, WebSocket message), each outbound fetch, and each cell start; the flush and sampling env vars control the pipeline.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/telemetry.md#L35-L50",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3a2ef719d398485d5dc63965b3d55230e3fd4a9d8982d53d37d8e4f51f69dee1:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_93034dbf029042769a636df1e8744f88",
+      "statement": "Each console.log line is recorded as a log record carrying the trace id and span id of the handler that wrote it, so a query can join logs to traces and the correlation survives await.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/telemetry.md#L42-L46",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:02aea8ea5c09230fedb41b88ba347c9e8f06468c71a7ca376bc27dbcdbe3fa79:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_778e67af03b348e7bf30ad3222672647",
+      "statement": "celld reads the W3C traceparent header on incoming requests and sends traceparent on outbound fetch, and a Worker call to a Durable Object stays in one trace.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/telemetry.md#L46-L51",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a446ef91bebc89179fe070cffe72abd2159ace461b5d551f54d95e402155434b:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_c7912eaaa73a48998d938dc7af25f23d",
+      "statement": "The hot path never blocks: record is a try_send, a full channel increments a drop counter, and encoding runs on spawn_blocking, so under saturation celld sheds telemetry counted but never sheds requests.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/telemetry.md#L50-L55",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:18439420630fdadba3a4abf0970fbf6effcfb6e485f47e195845100e64a45ba8:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_8e276ac7253f4b368daf9429c6b3092a",
+      "statement": "Parquet files are partitioned by node and hour under telemetry/traces/<node>/<yyyy>/<mm>/<dd>/<hh>/<id>.parquet, so a query of one day touches only that day's files.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/telemetry.md#L87-L89",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:962ab3d8430cab10740a6ed54521c76ed35495f69d8cc34d47adb33345e25b34:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_ce6c98f2096f4acd8d03d92f9c921e1f",
+      "statement": "One Parquet file is written per flush on the time or size limit whichever is reached first (defaults 5 minutes and 5 MB), and a query sees an event up to 5 minutes after the request at the defaults.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/telemetry.md#L93-L107",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9cd8d49a6fb8bfe06fc44f8bc2ad8b4a6e34814e9b0cf413d20af873ebd27896:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_4ae2e3b137a74735ad182ce73b95a80c",
+      "statement": "celld does not compact its own telemetry files; a compaction job on a maintenance node rewrites one past hour of small files into one large sorted zstd file per node/hour, rewrites only the hour that just ended, and never compacts the current hour a node still writes",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/telemetry.md#L112-L134",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7b0e44941f12e40a93fa9e63eb8402a4e183b4fdfcade9f08a11084ec1ca23d8:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_320665d711ee4de8ae96719269482a4c",
+      "statement": "The OTLP sink is hand-encoded protobuf to keep prost, tonic, and generated proto crates out of the binary, following field numbers from opentelemetry-proto v1.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/otlp.rs#L8-L16",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:72595840fb918186732eb29ef391e5ef703e3772c654982ed01c7a25cd748e82:"
+        }
+      ]
+    }
+  ],
+  "verification": {
+    "by": "openwiki/0.4.3",
+    "at": "2026-09-12T21:30:17.310Z"
+  }
+}

Index: openwiki/.claims/testing.json
===================================================================
--- openwiki/.claims/testing.json	
+++ openwiki/.claims/testing.json	
@@ -0,0 +1,124 @@
+{
+  "schemaVersion": 1,
+  "pageVersion": "sha256:1a8250efdd94e957713c4d47e3f7e32a11d73afea244cf7a25ba91d53061b911",
+  "claims": [
+    {
+      "id": "claim_9e11bb72977644249752f46b28cf3b3e",
+      "statement": "celld validates three promises — an acknowledged write is durable, a cell has one writer at a time, and Cloudflare Workers/Durable Objects code operates the same on celld — by breaking each at the layer where the failure shows most clearly.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/testing.md#L3-L14",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3c4a1ecc98a4e3b13bb5b488fdb636de9b3cefdc98834259b5ddf7d5a78d462b:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_c5df248f4fc64cde9c7251b3b5a7ff70",
+      "statement": "The compatibility promise is tested differentially: each program runs once on workerd and once on celld on identical bytes and the outputs must be equal, so a test cannot agree with celld's own runtime by accident.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/testing.md#L17-L27",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:678091183117ff8515f5ec015a3b2e907d55ec7624020ec1c47f63ddb6fed517:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_95e8643056434b63990d044c08f21231",
+      "statement": "The conformance corpus only grows: new API surfaces add fixtures that must give equal output on workerd and celld, and the suites build into the binary under celld_internal_tests via include! in crates/celld/lib.rs.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/lib.rs#L365-L430",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bd3916287ba0c544930c2b0605223dbf739ee7c51b09e2ea2834e98786640462:"
+        },
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/testing.md#L27-L32",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f3ec8371b63e27f4b551340c5ac549a4710d58c1199cd8697cb24e4112bd156b:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_956d3005d3f941a48a5572a68dabbd65",
+      "statement": "The coordination protocol is specified in TLA+ and exhaustively model-checked at a small configuration, visiting every reachable state with a linearizable store and perfect clocks; the invariants are one writer per epoch and no acknowledged write lost.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
